# ==============================================================================
# HOSTEL COMPLAINT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM - ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================
# Follow these 3 simple steps to connect Supabase:
# 1. Sign up or log into https://supabase.com and create a new project.
# 2. Run the provided 'supabase_schema.sql' in the Supabase SQL Editor.
# 3. Go to Project Settings -> API, copy Project URL & anon/public key, and paste below:
# ==============================================================================

# Your Supabase Project URL (e.g., https://xyzcompany.supabase.co)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co

# Your Supabase Anon Public Key (safe to expose in client-side code)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.your-anon-key-here

# Optional: Master Passcode for Hostel Warden / Admin Dashboard access
# Default fallback passcode is: warden2026
VITE_ADMIN_PASSCODE=warden2026

# ==============================================================================
# HOSTEL CONFIGURATION REFERENCE:
# Supported Hostel Blocks:
#   - Boys Hostel 1
#   - Boys Hostel 2
#   - Girls Hostel 1
#   - Girls Hostel 2
#
# Form Fields Captured:
#   - Student Full Name
#   - Student Phone / WhatsApp Number (used for updates & rate limiting)
#   - Student Roll Number / ID
#   - Hostel Block & Room Number (e.g. 104, B-204)
#   - Complaint Type (Maintenance, Electrical, Plumbing, Carpentry, WiFi, etc.)
#   - Category (Room Maintenance, Common Area, Washroom, Mess, etc.)
#   - Urgency Level (Low, Normal, High, Emergency)
#   - Image Upload (Optional photo attachment stored in 'complaint-attachments' bucket)
# ==============================================================================
